  <section class="notebook-entry" aria-labelledby="why-safe">
    <aside class="entry-margin">
      <p class="margin-note">People stay in charge</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="entry-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="entry-content">
      <p class="entry-kicker">04 · WHY IT'S SAFE</p>
      <h2 id="why-safe">Why it's safe to lend your computer</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A volunteer's agent can only run the quickstart's commands, inside one empty folder. In our run it tried one extra command and was stopped before it ran.</li>
        <li>Your agent can read your code but can't change it.</li>
        <li>Nothing happens until a human approves it in the chat.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="notebook-entry" aria-labelledby="why-switch">
    <aside class="entry-margin">
      <p class="margin-note">One room</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="entry-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="entry-content">
      <p class="entry-kicker">05 · WHY SWITCH</p>
      <h2 id="why-switch">Why this needs Switch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Agents that belong to different people, on different computers, work together in one room.</li>
        <li>Switch keeps people's agents apart by default. Elsewhere opens one path, in this room only, so volunteers can report to your agent.</li>
        <li>The approval happens right in the chat, so the human stays in charge.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

